<gallery>
File:Kaina Shrine Kou Kasugai Fuefuki City, Main hall.JPG|Main Hall
File:Kaina Shrine Kou Kasugai Fuefuki City, Oratory.JPG|Oratory
</gallery>

=== Kaina Shrine (Hashitate, Fuefuki) ===
{{Infobox shrine
| name        = Kaina Shrine
| image       = [[File:甲斐奈神社 (笛吹市一宮町橋立) 拝殿斜め.JPG|250px]]
| address     = 84 Hashitate, Fuefuki City, Yamanashi Prefecture
| coordinates = {{Coord|35|38|50.33|N|138|40|45.71|E|region:JP-19_type:landmark|display=inline,title}}
| deities     = {{ill|Kuninotokotachi|ja|国之常立尊}}, {{ill|Takami Musubi|ja|高皇産霊尊}}, {{ill|Izanagi|ja|伊弉諾尊}}, {{ill|Izanami|ja|伊弉冉尊}}
| status      = {{ill|Shikinaisha|ja|式内社}} contender, Sōja contender, former {{ill|Mura-sha|ja|村社}}
| founded     = 
| main_hall   = 
| othernames  = Jinsogu, Hashitate Daimyōjin
| festivals   = {{nihongo|March 23|3月23日}}
| rituals     = 
}}

This shrine, located in Hashitate, Fuefuki City, is another Ronsha contender. Its name, "Jinsogu," reflects its association with ancestral spirits or the provincial Sōja.

==== Deities ====
* {{ill|Kuninotokotachi|ja|国之常立尊}}
* {{ill|Takami Musubi|ja|高皇産霊尊}}
* {{ill|Izanagi|ja|伊弉諾尊}}
* {{ill|Izanami|ja|伊弉冉尊}}

==== History ====
Located near other provincial landmarks like the {{ill|Kai Kokubun-ji|ja|甲斐国分寺}} and {{ill|Kai Kokubun-niji|ja|甲斐国分尼寺}}, this site has long been associated with the administrative center of ancient Kai Province.

