<gallery>
File:甲斐奈神社 (笛吹市一宮町橋立) 本殿.JPG|Main Hall
File:甲斐奈神社 (笛吹市一宮町橋立) 拝殿.JPG|Oratory
File:甲斐奈神社 (笛吹市一宮町橋立) 大杉跡.JPG|Remains of the "Hashitate Great Cedar"
</gallery>

=== Kaina Shrine (Kofu) ===
{{Infobox shrine
| name        = Kaina Shrine
| image       = [[File:Kaina Shrine Kofu City,from the road outside.JPG|250px]]
| address     = 3-7-11 Chūō, Kofu City, Yamanashi Prefecture
| coordinates = {{Coord|35|39|40.47|N|138|34|41.35|E|region:JP-19_type:landmark|display=inline,title}}
| deities     = {{ill|Kukurihime no Mikoto|ja|菊理姫命}}, {{ill|Konohana Sakuya Hime|ja|木花咲耶姫命}}
| status      = {{ill|Shikinaisha|ja|式内社}} contender, former {{ill|Gōsha|ja|郷社}}
| founded     = Reign of {{ill|Emperor Suizei|ja|綏靖天皇}}
| main_hall   = 
| othernames  = Shirayama Gongen
| festivals   = {{nihongo|April 15|4月15日}}
| rituals     = 
}}

This shrine is located in Kofu City and is linked to the ancient Shirayama faith. It has been known by various names, including "Shirayama Gongen."

==== Deities ====
; Main Deities
* {{ill|Kukurihime no Mikoto|ja|菊理姫命}}
* {{ill|Konohana Sakuya Hime|ja|木花咲耶姫命}}
; Associated Deities
* {{ill|Ninigi|ja|瓊瓊杵命}}
* {{ill|Ōyamatsumi|ja|大山祇命}}
* {{ill|Iwanyakahime|ja|石長姫命}}

==== History ====
Originally located on {{ill|Atago-yama|ja|愛宕山 (甲府市)}} in Kofu, the shrine was relocated multiple times, eventually settling in its current location during the {{ill|Edo period|en}}.<ref name="chimei">{{Cite book|title=Yamanashi Prefecture Place Names|publisher=平凡社|year=1992}}</ref>

==== Gallery ====
<gallery>
File:Kaina Shrine Kofu City.JPG|Oratory
File:Kaina Shrine Kofu City, Main Hall.JPG|Main Hall
</gallery>

