In the {{ill|Sengoku period (Japan)|ja|戦国時代|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sengoku period (Japan)|qq=}}, the [[:en:Takeda clan|Takeda clan]] established the {{ill|Fuchū Hachiman Shrine|ja|府中八幡宮|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fuchū Hachiman Shrine|qq=}} in Kofu, which took over the role of the province's Sōja.
Debates over the Ronsha have persisted since the publication of the ''{{ill|Kai Koku-shi|ja|甲斐国志|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kai Koku-shi|qq=}}.'' Modern scholars, including those in the ''Shikinaisha Survey Report'' by Kogakkan University, remain undecided on the matter.<ref name="chosa"/>
=== Kaina Shrine (Kasugai, Fuefuki) === {{Infobox religious building| religious_affiliation = [[Shinto]] | name = Kaina Shrine | image = [[File:Kaina Shrine in Kou Kasugai, Fuefuki City.jpg|250px]] | location = 361 Kasugai, Fuefuki City, Yamanashi Prefecture | coordinates = {{Coord|35|39|39.65|N|138|39|03.69|E|region:JP-19_type:landmark|display=inline,title}} | deity = {{ill|Hoori|lt=Hoori|lt=Hikohohodemi no Mikoto|ja|彦火火出見尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hikohohodemi no Mikoto|qq=}}, {{ill|Ōkuninushi|ja|大己貴命|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōkuninushi|qq=}} | status = {{ill|Shikinaisha|ja|式内社|1=Shikinaisha|2=ja|3=式内社|qq=draft|1=Shikinaisha|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinaisha|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinaisha|qq=}} contender, "Fourth Shrine," Sōja contender, former {{ill|Mura-sha|ja|村社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Mura-sha|qq=}} | founded = | main_hall = | othernames = Shunomiya | festivals = {{nihongo|April 3|4月3日}} | rituals = }}
This shrine, located in Kasugai, Fuefuki City, is one of the primary Ronsha contenders. Its name, ''Shunomiya,'' suggests it may have served as either the "Fourth Shrine" or the provincial Sōja.<ref name="chosa"/>
==== Deities ==== * {{ill|Hoori|lt=Hoori|lt=Hikohohodemi no Mikoto|ja|彦火火出見尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hikohohodemi no Mikoto|qq=}} * {{ill|Ōkuninushi|ja|大己貴命|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōkuninushi|qq=}}
==== History ==== The site is thought to correspond to one of the possible locations of the ancient Kai Province Government Office, as indicated by its name.
During the {{ill|Edo period|en|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Edo period|qq=}}, the shrine was known as "Shunomiya" or "Shunomiya Daimyōjin." Some scholars interpret this as a variant of "Fourth Shrine" or "Guardian Shrine" (indicating a Sōja).<ref name="chosa"/>
