'''Kaina Shrine''' ({{lang|ja|甲斐奈神社}}, ''Kaina Jinja'') refers to a group of {{ill|Shinto shrine|en|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shinto shrine|qq=}} with the name "Kaina" located in [[:en:Yamanashi Prefecture|Yamanashi Prefecture]], Japan. There are three such shrines, all of which are {{ill|Shikinaisha|ja|式内社|1=Shikinaisha|2=ja|3=式内社|qq=draft|1=Shikinaisha|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinaisha|13=User:Immanuelle|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyocho|lt=Shikinaisha}} listed in the {{ill|Engishiki|ja|延喜式神名帳|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Engishiki|13=User:Immanuelle/Engishiki Jinmyōchō|qq=}} under "Kaina Shrine, Yamanashi District, Kai Province."
== Overview == The three Kaina Shrines are {{ill|Shikinaisha|ja|式内社|1=Shikinaisha|2=ja|3=式内社|qq=draft|1=Shikinaisha|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinaisha|13=User:Immanuelle|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyocho|lt=Shikinaisha}} contenders ({{ill|Ronsha|ja|論社|1=candidate shrines|2=ja|3=論社|lt=candidate|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ronsha|13=User:Immanuelle/candidate shrines|1=Engishiki_Jinmyōchō#Ronsha|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki_Jinmyocho|lt=Ronsha}}}}), meaning their historical authenticity as the original shrine listed in the ''Engishiki'' is debated. In total, there are four contenders for the title:
1. '''{{ill|Kaina Shrine (Fuefuki, Kasugai)|ja|甲斐奈神社 (笛吹市春日居町国府)|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kaina Shrine (Fuefuki, Kasugai)|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki link invalid}}''' (Kasugai, Fuefuki City) - Associated with [[:en:Kai Province|Kai Province]]'s [[:en:Sōja shrine|Sōja]] and considered the "Fourth Shrine" of the province. Former {{ill|Gōsha|ja|郷社|lt=Ken-sha|1=Modern_system_of_ranked_Shinto_shrines#District_shrine|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Gōsha|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 近代社格制度}}. 2. '''{{ill|Kaina Shrine (Fuefuki, Hashitate)|ja|甲斐奈神社 (笛吹市一宮町橋立)|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kaina Shrine (Fuefuki, Hashitate)|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki link invalid}}''' (Hashitate, Fuefuki City) - Another Sōja contender, formerly a {{ill|Mura-sha|ja|村社|lt=Son-sha|1=Modern_system_of_ranked_Shinto_shrines#Village_shrines|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Mura-sha|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 近代社格制度}}. 3. '''{{ill|Kaina Shrine (Kofu)|ja|甲斐奈神社 (甲府市)|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kaina Shrine (Kofu)|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 甲斐奈神社}}''' (Kofu City) - Former Gō-sha. 4. '''Azumaya-no-Miya''' (Chinme, Fuefuki City) - A {{ill|Sessha|ja|摂社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sessha|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 摂末社}} of {{ill|Yamanashioka Shrine|ja|山梨岡神社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yamanashioka Shrine|qq=}}.
The shifting locations of the {{ill|Kai Province Government Office|ja|甲斐国府|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kai Province Government Office|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki link invalid}}—from Kasugai to the vicinity of Hashitate, and eventually to Kofu—may explain the presence of multiple contenders for the Sōja title. The name "Kaina" could derive from "Kai no" ("of Kai Province") or other interpretations such as "Kai no Na" ("Kai's greens").<ref name="chosa">{{Cite book|title=Shikinaisha Survey Report|publisher=皇學館大学出版部|year=1985}}</ref><ref>Alternative interpretations suggest "Kaina" could mean "Kai's vegetables." (''Shikinaisha Survey Report'')</ref>
In the {{ill|Sengoku period (Japan)|ja|戦国時代|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sengoku period (Japan)|qq=}}, the [[:en:Takeda clan|Takeda clan]] established the {{ill|Fuchū Hachiman Shrine|ja|府中八幡宮|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fuchū Hachiman Shrine|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 国府八幡宮}} in Kofu, which took over the role of the province's Sōja.
Debates over the Ronsha have persisted since the publication of the ''{{ill|Kai Koku-shi|ja|甲斐国志|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kai Koku-shi|qq=}}.'' Modern scholars, including those in the ''Shikinaisha Survey Report'' by Kogakkan University, remain undecided on the matter.<ref name="chosa"/>
=== Kaina Shrine (Kasugai, Fuefuki) === {{Infobox religious building| religious_affiliation = [[Shinto]] | name = Kaina Shrine | image = [[File:Kaina Shrine in Kou Kasugai, Fuefuki City.jpg|250px]] | location = 361 Kasugai, Fuefuki City, Yamanashi Prefecture | coordinates = {{Coord|35|39|39.65|N|138|39|03.69|E|region:JP-19_type:landmark|display=inline,title}} | deity = {{ill|Hoori|lt=Hoori|lt=Hikohohodemi no Mikoto|ja|彦火火出見尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hikohohodemi no Mikoto|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to ホオリ}}, {{ill|Ōkuninushi|ja|大己貴命|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōkuninushi|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 大国主}} | status = {{ill|Shikinaisha|ja|式内社|1=Shikinaisha|2=ja|3=式内社|qq=draft|1=Shikinaisha|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinaisha|13=User:Immanuelle|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyocho|lt=Shikinaisha}} contender, "Fourth Shrine," Sōja contender, former {{ill|Mura-sha|ja|村社|lt=Son-sha|1=Modern_system_of_ranked_Shinto_shrines#Village_shrines|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Mura-sha|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 近代社格制度}} | founded = | main_hall = | othernames = Shunomiya | festivals = {{nihongo|April 3|4月3日}} | rituals = }}
This shrine, located in Kasugai, Fuefuki City, is one of the primary Ronsha contenders. Its name, ''Shunomiya,'' suggests it may have served as either the "Fourth Shrine" or the provincial Sōja.<ref name="chosa"/>
==== Deities ==== * {{ill|Hoori|lt=Hoori|lt=Hikohohodemi no Mikoto|ja|彦火火出見尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hikohohodemi no Mikoto|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to ホオリ}} * {{ill|Ōkuninushi|ja|大己貴命|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōkuninushi|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 大国主}}
==== History ==== The site is thought to correspond to one of the possible locations of the ancient Kai Province Government Office, as indicated by its name.
During the {{ill|Edo period|en|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Edo period|qq=}}, the shrine was known as "Shunomiya" or "Shunomiya Daimyōjin." Some scholars interpret this as a variant of "Fourth Shrine" or "Guardian Shrine" (indicating a Sōja).<ref name="chosa"/>
==== Gallery ==== <gallery> File:Kaina Shrine Kou Kasugai Fuefuki City, Main hall.JPG|main hall File:Kaina Shrine Kou Kasugai Fuefuki City, Oratory.JPG|Oratory </gallery>
=== Kaina Shrine (Hashitate, Fuefuki) === {{Infobox religious building| religious_affiliation = [[Shinto]] | name = Kaina Shrine | image = [[File:甲斐奈神社 (笛吹市一宮町橋立) 拝殿斜め.JPG|250px]] | location = 84 Hashitate, Fuefuki City, Yamanashi Prefecture | coordinates = {{Coord|35|38|50.33|N|138|40|45.71|E|region:JP-19_type:landmark|display=inline,title|qq=draft|qq=draft}} | deity = {{ill|Kuni-no-Tokotachi|lt=Kuni-no-Tokotachi|lt=Kuninotokotachi|ja|国之常立尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kuninotokotachi|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki link invalid}}, {{ill|Takami Musubi|ja|高皇産霊尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Takami Musubi|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to タカミムスビ}}, {{ill|Izanagi|ja|伊弉諾尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Izanagi|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to イザナギ}}, {{ill|Izanami|ja|伊弉冉尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Izanami|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to イザナミ}} | status = {{ill|Shikinaisha|ja|式内社|1=Shikinaisha|2=ja|3=式内社|qq=draft|1=Shikinaisha|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinaisha|13=User:Immanuelle|1=Engishiki Jinmyōchō|2=ja|3=延喜式神名帳|4=zh|5=延喜式神名帳|6=simple|7=Engishiki Jinmyocho|lt=Shikinaisha}} contender, Sōja contender, former {{ill|Mura-sha|ja|村社|lt=Son-sha|1=Modern_system_of_ranked_Shinto_shrines#Village_shrines|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Mura-sha|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 近代社格制度}} | founded = | main_hall = | othernames = Jinsogu, Hashitate Daimyōjin | festivals = {{nihongo|March 23|3月23日}} | rituals = }}
This shrine, located in Hashitate, Fuefuki City, is another Ronsha contender. Its name, "Jinsogu," reflects its association with ancestral spirits or the provincial Sōja.
==== Deities ==== * {{ill|Kuni-no-Tokotachi|lt=Kuni-no-Tokotachi|lt=Kuninotokotachi|ja|国之常立尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kuninotokotachi|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki link invalid}} * {{ill|Takami Musubi|ja|高皇産霊尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Takami Musubi|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to タカミムスビ}} * {{ill|Izanagi|ja|伊弉諾尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Izanagi|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to イザナギ}} * {{ill|Izanami|ja|伊弉冉尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Izanami|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to イザナミ}}
==== History ==== Located near other provincial landmarks like the [[:en:Kai Kokubun-ji|Kai Kokubun-ji]] and {{ill|Kai Kokubun-niji|ja|甲斐国分尼寺|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kai Kokubun-niji|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki link invalid}}, this site has long been associated with the administrative center of ancient Kai Province.
