This shrine, located in Hashitate, Fuefuki City, is another Ronsha contender. Its name, "Jinsogu," reflects its association with ancestral spirits or the provincial Sōja.

==== Deities ====
* {{ill|Kuni-no-Tokotachi|lt=Kuni-no-Tokotachi|lt=Kuninotokotachi|ja|国之常立尊|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kuninotokotachi|ja_comment=jawiki link invalid}}
* {{ill|Takami Musubi|ja|高皇産霊尊|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Takami Musubi|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to タカミムスビ|1=Takamimusubi|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q125400}}
* {{ill|Izanagi|ja|伊弉諾尊|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Izanagi|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to イザナギ}}
* {{ill|Izanami|ja|伊弉冉尊|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Izanami|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to イザナミ|1=Izanami|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q682306}}

==== History ====
Located near other provincial landmarks like the {{ill|Kai Kokubun-ji|en|Kai Kokubun-ji|qid=Q11577870|lt=Kai Kokubun-ji|1=Kai Kokubun-ji}} and {{ill|Kai Kokubun-niji|ja|甲斐国分尼寺|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kai Kokubun-niji|ja_comment=jawiki link invalid}}, this site has long been associated with the administrative center of ancient Kai Province.

